<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Banc One raised to buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Banc One raised to buy.</headline>
<text>
<p>- Keefe, Bruyette &amp; Woods Inc said on Monday it raised Banc One to buy from hold after the Columbus, Ohio-based bank said it plans to acquire credit card issuer First USA Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;We moved our rating up to buy with the selloff (as Banc One's share price declined 3-1/2 to 41-5/8 on the New York Stock Exchange),&quot; analyst Joseph Duwan said in a telephone interview. &quot;We think the market overreacted a little bit.&quot;</p>
<p>He trimmed his 1997 earnings estimate to $3.35 from $3.65 versus $3.23. The the bank said it sees about seven percent dilution in 1997. But Duwan left his $4.00 1998 estimate intact and said long-term earnings growth is enhanced.</p>
<p>((Cleveland Newsdesk, Susan Zimmerman 216-579-0077))</p>
